 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 543349,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Name three edges that you could remove from Graph <i>V</i> in Figure 12.225 to form a third spanning tree, different from those in the solution to Example 12.51 Exercise 3.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Remember that the number of edges in a tree graph with <i>n</i> vertices is <i>n</i> – 1.</p>\n<p>Graph V has 9 vertices and 11 edges. The associated spanning tree will have 8 edges. You need to remove 3 edges from Graph V.</p>\n<p>The example removed <i>ac, cf,</i> and <i>be</i>.</p>\n<p>You want to form a spanning tree by removing three edges. Keep in mind that you have to break up the three cycles, since a spanning tree cannot have any cycles.</p>\n<p>The three edges must include one edge from list A and a pair of edges from list B.</p>\n<p>List A: <i>be, eh, hi, gi, bg</i></p>\n<p>List B: <i>ac</i> and <i>ad</i>, <i>ac</i> and <i>af, ac</i> and <i>cd, ac</i> and <i>cf, ad</i> and <i>af, ad</i> and <i>cd, ad</i> and <i>cf, af</i> and <i>cd, af</i> and <i>cf</i>, or <i>cd</i> and <i>cf</i></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The three edges must include one edge from list A and one pair of edges from list B.\n<br>\nList A: <i>be</i>, <i>eh</i>, <i>hi</i>, <i>gi</i>, <i>bg</i>\n<br>\nList B: <i>ac</i> and <i>ad</i>, <i>ac</i> and <i>af</i>, <i>ac</i> and <i>cd</i>, <i>ac</i> and <i>cf</i>, <i>ad</i> and <i>af</i>, <i>ad</i> and <i>cd</i>, <i>ad</i> and <i>cf</i>, <i>af</i> and <i>cd</i>, <i>af</i> and <i>cf</i>, or <i>cd</i> and <i>cf</i>."
    }
   ],
